From 34e0eb0ceef7f6bd0df0b7f390c5c4ddbcc138ef Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Angelo Arifi <arifilabs@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 6 Oct 2026 10:49:03 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] lane-302: IQ4_NL gather byte-pair LUT + IQ3_S gather batched
 grid init arms (opt-in)

GGML_ARIFI_IQ4NL_BODY=1: the IQ4_NL expert-gather mat-vec reads both nibble values of a qs byte with one LDS
read from a 256-entry vec2 table built from the 16-entry LUT (same floats, same dequantize4 component order,
byte-identical by construction); =3 is the planted wrong arm (pair swapped). Spec constant 4 of the idg pipeline.
GGML_ARIFI_IQ3S_INIT=1: the IQ3_S gather grid init issues all 8 per-thread loads before any LDS store (the IQ2_S
lever-4 shape, cellN-10060804 ISA 16 -> 2 serialized waits there); =2 is the planted wrong arm (table rotated).
Both unset = 0 = legacy; idg pipelines only, so n_tokens 1 is untouched. Gather notice prints both values.
Cherry-pick name for lane 298: lane-302 IQ4_NL/IQ3_S gather body arms.

Origin: lane-302 (ArifiLabs native, fork-authored; no upstream origin)
Measured-effect: OPT-IN, default off. Op level cells/cellQ-10061202-read.json (cache/moe-gather-x1-lane): IQ4_NL byte-pair LUT n2 +14.7/+15.8%, n4 +12.9/+15.6%, n8 +16.2/+19.5% slower; IQ3_S batched init n2 +10.2/+19.9%, n4 +3.7/+6.3% slower, n8 -1.8/-1.7%; both byte-identical (harness IDENT) with planted RED; default arm unchanged
